        <p>Mr. E. Imiaon took exception to till providing of uni• form for the caret 'ker. Mr. W. Handley explained that it ha i been consi lered by the Committee Chit it would add a great deal to the tme of the institution to hive tht official cloths in uni- form. Ile was the only official tkat had no Rulh uniform that 'ma occupying such a post for tho Council. A number of cases had been cited in which the caretaker had to answer the door in his "shirt sleeves." And num- bers of people aver, always enquiring. for the caretak.r. . Mr. Unison thought nothing would be gained by hw- in; till uniform. Possibly Mrs. Jackson had ansrrered the door filmy times in a "cotton cap" etc. (loughter.) He would object to the provision of uniform. On a vote being taken the recommendations were adopted Mr. Imison only objecting.</p>
        <p>THE LIBRARY.</p>
