        <p>This ancient Court was held at the Court Ft„- ton Castle, on Saturday atrerneoa. Th-re were pre,geat R Mert Davies, of Warriugt m, higia steward ; M Kirke innel, Mr. Sei,eph Walker, h,gla bailiff, ant the f 'Bowing representatives ot the va loos townships within th3juris licticia of the court :—appleton, Join Ellison;B artington,Jartvs Lowe; Daresbury,John Coop .r; Halton, Messrs. T. Wrignt, H. Raw", Jtha Lea, Je•eph Manning, and John Newport ' • Etat:eon, T. J. Weir ; Lymm, W. Mullard ; Miltingtoa, William Tnomas Brun- dritt; Newton-by-Daresoury, S. Basnett ; Prrston- Hill,John White ; Suttoo,John E. Bate ' • Stretcon„Jo ira Etlison ; Walton Sup 'riot, W. Weir and T:»33 as flici Burgess ; Walton Interior, Messre. Mauntie:d and Willi.- field. Tne court having beea opened with usual anci .ac forms, the following jury wee empannelled :—Messrs. Thomas Wright (f,d•nrt an), J. Edison Jaws Low-join Cooper, a Rowe, J.&amp; a be i, J. Manning. all John Newport. Taey were soleamiy charged to " laity enquire and make presentment ot all such mat-yes as relate t^ the present sirvics, wheraie they as mid spare no man through f a:., lots, favour, or affe eioa, present any man out ot malice or hatred." Mr. Davies said he cud only say how thankful he was t be able to meet them once again. fie looked for- ward to the meeting wan the greatest po s.ble pleaiere &amp;nine the year, because he saw acme faces that he did not otherwise see. He was thankful to be spared afar to be in nett sr health than 119 %V is. (Hear, hair, and ap- planes.) As ShakeT rare said, he had a silent ro,raw wnich did not 9.1447419 199473 WM. At the Caine time he though-. it right ser-ous V ti tiapress his ihankfuln-ss to wet them again an i in fair health. They all knew with reference te that wall.; they had in the record offics the proceedings that were signed by people of the 9i-me name as some of those present that day ia 1220, so that thes3 courts mast have existed something like 650 years. When