        <p>Conaiderable jet ,rest is cenlered in the forthcoming School Board Election for the district of Runcomand in certain querters feeling runs vary high. A. fillip to the proceedmis is also given by the publication in the •• Runcorn Parish Magazine " of the hollowing extract , from the "Vicer's Letter." : " None of us, I suppose, whia to plunge into the uncertainty an expense ot a School Boar] contest, but tje elec in of a new Board which will consist of nine members, instead of seven, is cloae upon us, and it is desirable that all who wish to maintain tha7 frienliy condition nf Clings under which school affairs are manage I in this town, where ruinous competition between V euntary and Board Schools is non-existent, should he wide a wake,and talcs good care thae a new era of echo)] wariare is not inaugurated by restlees Oa Fri lay evening last there was a meeting of rate- payers held in the Bethesda Lecture Hall, presided over be Mr. F. J. Nor:nen, JP., at which meeting,we under- et ml, some strong expressions of opinion with regard to the c mititution of the future School Board for Rune corn were in luleed in, and at thee ril of which it was decided that five undenorninetional candidates should hr neminatei an I run ceni)iatlv—with the support of tha'. meeting—for seats on the Boari. Tee peek stion of the exteaf:t given above,ie presume ably nothing in ire nor less then the throwing d iwn of the gauntlet in the teeth of these "reetless spirits " who are so anxi ,11 to have me undelominalonal representa- tion oe thi Board.'[lie being gene-alv seoeen of as such, an I is a consequence • intense interest is being evincril in the fertheoming election.</p>
