        <p>New YORK, Tnuasnay. The following despa'ci has tot en ri-c.ived here from Santiago :—lt is rurnJured that the UAted States trans- port Panama, bound from this p..r. tor New York was wrecked off Cape Mays' on the lit inst., with 300 per- sons on board, of whom few escaped. Ic is reported that wreckage, boaring the ship's name, has been picked up by a filhermai. Cape Nlalsi 13 the extreme eastern p)int of Cuba, round wLicn the transport from Santiago have ro proceed through the Wind ward Passage on her way talnhward to New Yolk. No informati,n whatever has been received at the Navy Department of the reported foundering of the transport Panama.</p>
