        <p>PARIS, TIIIIRSDLY. Discussing the possibilities and the outlook ol the Fashoda affair, tie" Fi.44ro "regards the evacuation of the post sooner ur later with calmness since it must Lecessarity take place. The" Petit Journal " however, declares that Major Marchand' s retreat is tantamodat to th:. s ter.fice of all France's political and commercial intereks on the Nile Valley. The " Edair " threatens L -,rd Salisbury that h 3 will pay dearly for the triumpn ne desir,s to-day at the expensed France.</p>
