      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0075" n="art0075">
        <head>TIIE NOUTIIERN UNION.</head>
        <p>TIIE NOUTIIERN UNION.</p>
        <p>YORKSHIRE v. CEIE3FIIRE.</p>
        <p>In this mat;h--w-ac-h-c-a-Trie-off--;;;SI—a-t-I-ningham before 8,000 pcople, Gold thorpo oncne,l the teoripg by register- a penalty goal for the Ty ke;. fhu StrcliEfe added a try, but Saville ntaliated with a goal for the Ces- trians bfor tle interval. Dur.ng the course of ne second period, A. Rigg add !it two tries and Lumley one tu. the hone score, the re ult beichl a victory for York - shin by a goal and four. tries to a goal. Near the close of play Jolley, of Ch^shire, fraddrect a rib.</p>
