        <head>"(Signed) MRS. E. MILLS." Mothers in the weak slat 3 CV hich Mrs. Mills' igter-</head>
        <p>"(Signed) MRS. E. MILLS." Mothers in the weak slat 3 CV hich Mrs. Mills' igter-</p>
        <p>an even character. Parr gradually assume I the upper hand, and pressed the vtoitors backs some w's ot. F'soer kad an opening but he failed to seize the odoportuntty and the Parr forwards were driven bier. They wOoid take no denial and they nain rushed to tie attack,Chew having to save a warm shot from Goulding. Eirletitown took up the attiek, and one of the Parr hack i failing to stop the rush C. Lee scored for ths visitors the only goal of the game. Parr were on their mettle,and seeing two points vanishing, attacked strongly but Wilkinson re- lieved and at half time Parr had not succf eJel in break- ing through the defence. The second half of the game wag all in favour of the visitors who however were un- able owing tp the stubborn defen3e of Parr, ti iriareise their score, and the game ended in a win for Ealestown of 1 goal to nit.</p>
